WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:15.494
Nina saw Izzie on her way to Kids Central.

2
00:00:15.495 --> 00:00:19.050
"Want to see the book I got at the book fair today?

3
00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.320
It's called All About Fruit.

4
00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.704
I love fruit!"

5
00:00:23.705 --> 00:00:27.236
"I love fruit too!" Izzie said.

6
00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:31.021
Outside, Miss Shelly blew her whistle.

7
00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:34.970
"Girls, time to put the book away."

8
00:00:34.971 --> 00:00:40.954
"But we're reading about our favorite food. Fruit!" Nina said.

9
00:00:40.955 --> 00:00:45.908
Miss Shelly laughed. "Perfect.

10
00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:49.799
Because today we are going on a fruit picnic!

11
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.550
But first we have to make our fruit feast."

12
00:00:54.551 --> 00:00:58.729
"A fruit picnic? Yay!" Izzie said.

13
00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.846
"What's a fruit feast?

14
00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:04.435
It sounds yummy!" Nina said.

15
00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:07.672
"Jason, please read the menu."

16
00:01:07.673 --> 00:01:13.294
Miss Shelly pointed to a piece of paper tacked onto a tree trunk.

17
00:01:13.295 --> 00:01:18.123
"Fruit kebabs and kiwi-and-cream sandwiches," Jason read.

18
00:01:18.124 --> 00:01:23.308
"First we'll make the fruit kebabs," Miss Shelly told them.

19
00:01:23.309 --> 00:01:26.666
"What's a kebab?" Bobby asked.

20
00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:32.934
"A kebab is food on a skewer," Miss Shelly said.

21
00:01:32.935 --> 00:01:38.728
"So poke a skewer through four pieces of fruit."

22
00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:46.266
"Grape, melon, banana, apple!" Izzie put her fruit on a skewer.

23
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:51.779
"Melon, apple, banana, grape!" Jason said.

24
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.170
"Grape, grape, grape, grape," Bobby said.

25
00:01:56.171 --> 00:01:57.864
"Is that okay?"

26
00:01:57.865 --> 00:02:00.799
"Whatever you want is fine, Bobby.

27
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.754
It's your fruit kebab!

28
00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:10.402
When you're finished, put your kebab in a container," Miss Shelly said.

29
00:02:10.403 --> 00:02:16.452
"Now we'll make the kiwi-and-cream sandwiches," Miss Shelly said.

30
00:02:16.453 --> 00:02:18.987
"Take two slices of bread.

31
00:02:18.988 --> 00:02:23.797
Spread whipped cream on one side of each slice," Izzie read.

32
00:02:23.798 --> 00:02:28.650
"Then place some kiwi on one slice of bread," Bobby read.

33
00:02:28.651 --> 00:02:33.875
"Place the other slice of bread on top to complete your sandwich.

34
00:02:33.876 --> 00:02:38.506
Ta-da! I'm done." Nina held up her sandwich.

35
00:02:38.507 --> 00:02:41.940
"Now we prepare the picnic basket."

36
00:02:41.941 --> 00:02:44.369
Miss Shelly held up a basket.

37
00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.830
"Put your sandwich in a bag.

38
00:02:46.831 --> 00:02:54.651
Then put it in your container."

39
00:02:54.652 --> 00:02:57.801
"Off we go!" Miss Shelly said.

40
00:02:57.802 --> 00:03:03.777
The kids followed her onto the path through the woods.

41
00:03:03.778 --> 00:03:07.534
They stopped at a grassy area.

42
00:03:07.535 --> 00:03:11.006
"We made s'mores here!" Nina said.

43
00:03:11.007 --> 00:03:15.180
"Yes, and this is where we'll have our picnic too.

44
00:03:15.181 --> 00:03:18.356
What do you think?" Miss Shelly answered.

45
00:03:18.357 --> 00:03:25.033
"Great!" Bobby said.

46
00:03:25.034 --> 00:03:29.254
"Maybe we should have brought umbrellas," Nina said.

47
00:03:29.255 --> 00:03:31.280
Everyone looked at her.

48
00:03:31.281 --> 00:03:33.922
"Why?" Miss Shelly asked.

49
00:03:33.923 --> 00:03:36.154
Nina held out her palm.

50
00:03:36.155 --> 00:03:41.591
"Because I just felt a raindrop!"

51
00:03:41.592 --> 00:03:44.407
"Quick! Put the food back in the basket,"

52
00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:47.889
Miss Shelly said as it began to rain harder.

53
00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:52.614
"Don't forget your sit-upon!"

54
00:03:52.615 --> 00:04:00.322
"Oh no! My book!" Nina ran back for her book.

55
00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:06.249
"Whew, we made it." Miss Shelly stopped to catch her breath.

56
00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.129
"The rain stopped.

57
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.342
Look, the sun is coming out!" Nina said.

58
00:04:12.343 --> 00:04:17.024
"Oh, this weather." Miss Shelly sighed.

59
00:04:17.025 --> 00:04:18.690
Then she smiled.

60
00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:22.770
"Why don't we have our picnic here on the blacktop?"

61
00:04:22.771 --> 00:04:28.576
Izzie grinned. "If it starts to rain again, we can run back inside."

62
00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:32.133
She plopped her sit-upon down on the blacktop.

63
00:04:32.134 --> 00:04:34.016
"Anywhere is fine.

64
00:04:34.017 --> 00:04:37.194
Let's eat already," Nina said.

65
00:04:37.195 --> 00:04:42.896
"And then we can read my fruit book again!"

66
00:04:42.897 --> 00:04:54.936
[caption_out@
